ABC_SCRIPT: a design's own ABC script in place of the area or speed one

synth_preamble.tcl picks abc_area.script or abc_speed.script by ABC_AREA
and nothing else. A design that builds its buffer trees after synthesis
(bazel-orfs tools/fanout_tree) wants ABC to map for delay without
`buffer -c`, whose chains it would only take down again. ABC_SCRIPT, when
set, names the script to use instead; unset, nothing changes.

Carried, not upstreamed. Retires at a bump onto an ORFS that lets a design
name its ABC script.

diff --git a/flow/scripts/synth_preamble.tcl b/flow/scripts/synth_preamble.tcl
index ef142be..e61d4b2 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/synth_preamble.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/synth_preamble.tcl
@@ -203,6 +203,10 @@ if { $::env(ABC_AREA) } {
   puts "Using ABC speed script."
   set abc_script $::env(SCRIPTS_DIR)/abc_speed.script
 }
+if { [env_var_exists_and_non_empty ABC_SCRIPT] } {
+  puts "Using the design's ABC script $::env(ABC_SCRIPT)."
+  set abc_script $::env(ABC_SCRIPT)
+}
 
 # Create argument list for stat
 set lib_args ""
